<title>GERMANY: East German Sept adjusted unemployment up 4,000.</title>
<headline>East German Sept adjusted unemployment up 4,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Sep 96	 Aug 96	   Sep 95</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    1.099 million    1.123 million	1.033</p>
<p> Number (adj)		1.140 million    1.136 million	1.070</p>
<p> Change (adj)	     +4,000	 -12,000	   n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		14.7 pct     15.0 pct	 13.8 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	48,573	 47,501	   57,991</p>
<p> Vacancies		   58,831	 57,524	   55,734</p>
<p> Change in number in wrk Jul 96	 Jun 96</p>
<p>				+9,000	 +7,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Previously announced data in brackets. Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>--Bonn newsroom, 49-228-609750</p>
</text>
